WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.032
Deep learning rarely has one objective.

2
00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:06.130
Pruning pairs the task loss with a sparsity penalty.

3
00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.335
One loss is the deliverable, the other a constraint.

4
00:00:10.031 --> 00:00:12.922
Yet the usual methods treat them as equals.

5
00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:21.220
Priority-Constrained Descent, or PCD, follows the primary gradient, and bends away from it only as much as needed.

6
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:24.703
Directions that make enough progress on the secondary form a half-space.

7
00:00:25.516 --> 00:00:31.205
PCD keeps the primary gradient if it lies inside, and projects it there if not.

8
00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:40.092
On ResNet-34 with CIFAR-100, PCD keeps seventy point nine percent accuracy with ninety percent of the parameters removed.

9
00:00:40.788 --> 00:00:43.795
The strongest baseline reaches forty-four.

10
00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:49.029
The pruned network is almost ten times smaller, and almost three times faster on a CPU.

11
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:51.656
Not all objectives are born equal.

12
00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:54.338
Your optimizer shouldn't treat them as equals.
